From: OpenWrt MT6990 integration
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: add MT6990 frame-engine data

MT6990 uses its vendor-defined frame engine with two SGMII MACs and QDMA.
Describe it with MT6990-specific data and paths. The mainline NETSYS version
must not be used as a proxy for MT798x-compatible hardware behaviour.

Keep the new capability MT6990-specific.  This leaves all existing MediaTek
networking platforms unchanged.

Refreshed for Linux 6.18.55: MTK_SOC_MT6990_BIT now follows MTK_GMAC_EEE_BIT,
which stable 6.18.53 added (upstream d876c9cb2d16). The original patch also
carried mt6990_data and of_mtk_match hunks after a blank line that ended the
mtk_eth_soc.c section, so patch never applied them; they are dropped here
because 972a adds the same entries.

